  "root_cause": "All 25 paths are transitive through @opencode/plugin@2.3.2 -> @opencode/util@2.3.2 -> npm CLI libraries. The two named advisories are glob GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4 (AbortSignal cancellation bypass) and minimatch GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (globparts amplification). No high or critical advisory is present.",
  "reachability": {
    "result": "not reached by the plugin entry",
    "evidence": [
      "src/plugin.ts:4 imports Model, Plugin, and Provider from @opencode/plugin; those are schema exports plus an identity helper.",
      "node_modules/@opencode/plugin/dist/promise/index.js exports the schema modules and Plugin from ./plugin.js.",
      "node_modules/@opencode/plugin/dist/promise/plugin.js is only `export function define(plugin) { return plugin; }`.",
      "No file under node_modules/@opencode/plugin/dist/promise or dist/effect imports @opencode/util.",
      "src/tui.ts:21 imports the TUI type only; the import is erased and the runtime does not load @opencode/plugin/tui.",
      "node_modules/@opencode/util/dist/glob.js:1 imports glob, but the plugin never imports @opencode/util/glob. The host may load other util modules; that is outside this package entry."
    ],
    "caveat": "Static import graph, not a runtime module trace. A future import of @opencode/util or a host path that loads util/glob would change reachability."
  },
